# Studio lock files — always transient
*.rbxl.lock
*.rbxlx.lock

# NOTE: place files are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Workspace geometry is not Rojo-managed, so the world exists only in the
# place file. It is ~14,000 parts and cannot practically be regenerated from
# a builder script, so the place file IS the source of truth for everything
# under Workspace. See README, "Saving the world".
#
# RNGArmory.rbxl is binary: it stores fine in git but will not produce
# readable diffs, and two people editing the world at once cannot merge it.
# Coordinate before making world changes. If Studio ever offers .rbxlx (XML),
# prefer it — that format diffs.

# Rojo build output
build/
*.rbxm
*.rbxmx

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# UI source art (gear panel template and its upload-sized crops).
#
# Deliberately NOT committed. This repo is public and the artwork is a
# third-party UI kit (the mockup carries a "moon tribe" watermark), so its
# licence needs checking before it is redistributed here.
#
# Nothing in the game needs these files: the panel is referenced by uploaded
# asset id in AssetConfig.Images.GearPanel, and GearHudController cuts every
# gear icon out of that same uploaded asset at runtime. These are only needed
# to re-cut or re-upload the artwork.
inventory_ui_transparent*.png
armory-gear-panel*.png
gear.zip
